<VI _name="lvdqmh_add_module_data_fields.vi" description="Adds fields to a DQMH module's DATA CLUSTER typedef (Module Data--cluster.ctl) IN PLACE and saves it, so the module keeps its state on the Message Handling Loop's shift register instead of in a functional global variable (Hampel Soft DQMH conventions).\0A\0AEvery control on the Donor VI's front panel is copied into the typedef's cluster with Move (duplicate TRUE) - its label becomes the field name, its type the field type - and placed below the cluster's last element. The .ctl is opened in the ACTIVE PROJECT's application instance and saved in place, so it stays a member of the module's library\3A writing a new .ctl over it (lvai_create_typedef overwrite) drops that membership, and Main.vi then reports the typedef missing (measured 2026-11-12). Main.vi, which carries the typedef in its shift register constant, is saved afterwards so the files agree.">
